    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "When one-third of a number is added to three-quarters of a number, the result is 10 more than the number. Find the number.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "The number is $120$.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the number.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{3x}{4}&=x+10\\\\4x+9x&=12x+120\\\\13x&=12x+120\\\\x&=120\\end{align*}$$\nThe number is $120$.",
